From: valentin rameau <valentin.rameau@outlook.fr>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:44:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/33] Record emulation-mode transitions on the Vita host

In emulation mode the 65816 forces M and X to 8-bit, so a REP #$30 cannot
widen them and every following immediate decodes one byte short. Only XCE
enters that mode, and its opcode ($FB) also occurs as the operand of the
raster bands' BVC spin, so one mis-step into that byte flips the CPU into
emulation and corrupts everything after it.

Report the step either side of a flip, Vita-only, in the existing hook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c b/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c
index 48eae3e..787c17f 100644
--- a/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c
+++ b/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c
@@ -1844,6 +1844,23 @@ static int _interp_run_core(CpuState *cpu, uint32_t entry_pc24,
               if (s_prev_mapped && !_mapped)
                 interp_bridge_note_offrails_vita(s_prev_pc, s_prev_op, s_prev_sp,
                                                  pc_before, op);
+              /* Emulation-mode transitions. In emulation mode the 65816
+               * forces M and X to 8-bit, so a REP #$30 cannot widen them and
+               * every following immediate decodes one byte short. Only XCE
+               * ($FB) enters it, and $FB also appears as the operand of the
+               * bands' BVC spin -- so a single mis-step into that byte flips
+               * the CPU into emulation and corrupts everything after. Record
+               * the step that does it. */
+              { extern void interp_bridge_note_emulation_vita(
+                    uint32_t pc, uint8_t op, uint16_t sp, uint8_t to_e);
+                static int s_prev_e = -1;
+                int _e = in.e ? 1 : 0;
+                if (s_prev_e >= 0 && _e != s_prev_e)
+                  interp_bridge_note_emulation_vita(s_prev_pc, s_prev_op,
+                                                    in.sp, (uint8_t)_e);
+                s_prev_e = _e;
+              }
+
               /* Entries into the raster handler region $00:8601-$00:8680.
                * The host enters it only through bank_00_8601's AOT alias, so
                * an LLE step arriving here from outside names whatever other
